    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "In the first folder, \"Previous ruptures in GIS\", the rupture areas of the earthquakes in 1940, 1966, 1974, and 2007 occurring in the subduction zone along the Coast of Lina, Peru, are provided in a GIS format. The boundaries of the tectonic region of analysis shown in black in Figure 1 in Ceferino et al. (2020) are also provided in GIS format. In the second folder \"Scripts\", Matlab scripts to reproduce the rupture simulation in Ceferino et al. (2020) are provided. In the third folder \"Consistency Simulation\", the file with the Supplemental Figures S1 to S6 showing the consistency of the model in all fault sections for different spatial correlations can be found.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Ceferino, Luis and Kiremidjian, Anne and Deierlein, Gregory. (2020). Earthquake rupture data and Matlab scripts from: Ceferino L., Kiremidjian, A., and Deierlein, G. Probabilistic space- and time-interaction modeling of mainshock earthquake rupture occurrence. Bulletin of Seismological Society of America (2020). Stanford Digital Repository. Available at: https://purl.stanford.edu/fk828tc8567",
